# Licence Verification Checklist

Use this checklist once the actual licence documents are in hand. It replaces the reference frameworks (RF-A, RF-B) with the terms that really apply. Complete one copy per font family, or per licence where one licence covers several fonts.

Record the answer, the clause reference and the evidence ID for every item. Where the documents are silent, write "silent" rather than leaving the item blank; silence is itself a finding when the licence reserves all rights not expressly granted.

---

## Part A. Identify the governing documents

| # | Question | Answer | Clause / evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| A1 | Which font family, styles and file formats does this licence cover? | | |
| A2 | Who is the licensor (foundry, Monotype, reseller)? Who sold it (Monotype, MyFonts, agency, other)? | | |
| A3 | Who is the licensee entity? Is it NovaWear, an individual employee, a former employee, or an agency? | | |
| A4 | What documents make up the licence (EULA, order form, invoice, account terms, amendments, side letters)? | | |
| A5 | Which version of the EULA applied on the date of acceptance? Is that version available? | | |
| A6 | How and when was the licence accepted (click-through, signed order form, purchase)? | | |
| A7 | Is the licence perpetual, annual or subscription-based? What are the start, end and renewal dates? | | |
| A8 | Is any order of precedence stated between the EULA, order form and other terms? | | |

## Part B. Grant and volume limits

| # | Question | Answer | Clause / evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| B1 | What desktop rights are granted? How are users or workstations counted (named, concurrent, potential access)? How many are licensed? | | |
| B2 | Are server or cloud installations permitted? On what access conditions? | | |
| B3 | Is web use granted? Self-hosting or licensor-hosting? Measured how (page views, domains)? Licensed volume? | | |
| B4 | Is application embedding granted? Measured how (apps, downloads, registered or active users)? Licensed volume? | | |
| B5 | Is use in emails and digital ads granted? Measured how (impressions, opens)? Licensed volume? | | |
| B6 | What may be embedded in documents (PDF, PPTX)? Are editable embeddings allowed? Any restriction on commercial documents? | | |
| B7 | Are static images, printed goods and merchandise expressly permitted, restricted or not mentioned? | | |
| B8 | Is there a distinction between prototype or internal use and production or deployment use? If so, how is a font designated for production? | | |
| B9 | Is the grant limited by territory? | | |

## Part C. Third parties

| # | Question | Answer | Clause / evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| C1 | May agencies, contractors or freelancers use the font on the licensee's behalf? Are they counted? | | |
| C2 | May font files be given to them, or must they hold their own licence? | | |
| C3 | Is sublicensing permitted? To whom and on what conditions? | | |
| C4 | What is the position for commercial printers? | | |
| C5 | May affiliates or subsidiaries use the font? | | |

## Part D. Restrictions

| # | Question | Answer | Clause / evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| D1 | Is format conversion (for example OTF to WOFF2) prohibited or permitted? | | |
| D2 | Is modification, subsetting or renaming restricted? | | |
| D3 | Are there restrictions on use in logos, trade marks or products for resale? | | |
| D4 | Is use in authoring tools, templates or user-customisable products restricted? | | |
| D5 | Are there backup-copy limits? | | |
| D6 | Are there restrictions on use with automated or machine-learning processes? | | |

## Part E. Compliance mechanics

| # | Question | Answer | Clause / evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| E1 | Is the licensee required to report use (for example, quarterly)? | | |
| E2 | Does the licensor have audit, inspection or certification rights? Notice period? Who bears costs? | | |
| E3 | What happens if limits are exceeded (true-up, additional fees, termination)? | | |
| E4 | On termination or expiry, what happens to fonts installed and materials already created or distributed? | | |
| E5 | Is there a cure period before termination? | | |

## Part F. Law and disputes

| # | Question | Answer | Clause / evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| F1 | Which law governs the licence? | | |
| F2 | Which courts or arbitral forum have jurisdiction? | | |
| F3 | Are there limitation-of-liability, indemnity or liquidated-damages provisions? | | |
| F4 | Does the licence state duration and territory? (Relevant to s. 19(5) and (6) of the Copyright Act, applied to licences by s. 30A.) | | |
| F5 | Does the licence characterise unlicensed use as infringement, breach or both? | | |

